Specifically inherited from ccbot's terminal_parser.py:
  - The UIPattern dataclass shape (name + top/bottom regex tuples + min_gap)
  - The _try_extract iteration algorithm
  - The initial set of UI_PATTERNS regex definitions
  - The parse_status_line skeleton (chrome separator + spinner scan)
  - The STATUS_SPINNERS character set

Original to this package (and its predecessor ccmux-backend by the same
author):
  - The ClaudeState sealed union (Working / Idle / Blocked / Dead)
  - The parse_pane top-level classifier
  - The walkback mechanism for tool-preview extraction
  - Pattern-drift detection with fingerprinted dedup
  - The OVERLAY vs TODO skippable-pattern split
  - Completion-summary filtering ("Worked for 56s" classifies as Idle)
  - The user override system (parser_config.json + CLAUDE_CODE_STATE_DIR)

